  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Engagement Support (SES) - USAID</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Azerbaijan):  .FY 2021 resources will be used to support a forthcoming governance activity entitled Social Engagement Support (SES), building off of the ten-year Socio-Economic Development Activity, to be awarded by the end of FY 2021.  The SES activity will be a five-year, approximately$15M activity geared towards fostering citizen-government dialogue to address local issues, reduce community vulnerabilities, and increase community resilience to identified sources of vulnerability, including those of a socio-economic nature.  USAID will seek to integrate the Agency&apos;s private sector engagement approach to include the private sector as a critical stakeholder in community dialogues with local government and central level government as appropriate.  The new activity will utilize a community-engagement approach that prioritizes democratic governance and will leverage private sector networks and resources to enhance access to quality and sustainable service delivery.  The activity will support rural Azerbaijani citizens to become increasingly independent (ICS Goal 3.1), promote stability in vulnerable areas (ICS Goal 1.2, JSP 1.3), and grow an increasingly productive rural economy (ICS Goal 2.2, JSP 2.2). .</narrative>
  </description>
